# Mannerly App Distribution, Store Setup, and Web Launch

Mannerly should operate as one platform distributed through several storefronts rather than as separate products. The same account, learner profile, progress, Mannerly Passport, subscriptions, family relationships, classrooms, regions, languages, and purchases should ultimately sync through one backend regardless of whether the user enters through iPhone, Android, Fire Tablet, Windows, or the web.

The primary launch platforms should be **Apple App Store, Google Play, and the Mannerly website/web application**. Amazon Appstore should be the next priority if Fire Tablet users become important to the family and child audience. Samsung Galaxy Store, Huawei AppGallery, and Microsoft Store should be secondary distribution channels added when their audiences justify the additional testing, billing, support, and release work.

## One Mannerly Account Everywhere

A user should be able to create a Mannerly account on an iPhone, sign into the web application later, and see the same profile and progress. A parent should be able to manage children's profiles from a computer while those children learn on tablets. A teacher should be able to create assignments from the web dashboard while students complete those assignments through Android, iOS, or a browser.

The platform should therefore treat Apple, Google, Amazon, Samsung, Huawei, Microsoft, and the web as **distribution and payment surfaces**, not independent account databases.

Authentication should connect to the central Mannerly backend. The backend should own learner profiles, household relationships, classrooms, home-region access, purchased Travel Packs, lesson progress, achievements, accessibility preferences, and subscription entitlements.

Store-specific systems should primarily handle downloading the application and, where applicable, purchasing digital subscriptions or content.

## Create the Business Accounts First

Before publishing, Mannerly should establish developer accounts under the actual Mannerly business entity where possible rather than tying the entire business permanently to a founder's personal developer identity.

For Apple organization enrollment, Apple requires organization verification information including a D-U-N-S Number, an organization-associated work email, and a functional public website tied to the organization.

Google also distinguishes between personal and organization developer accounts. Organization verification can require a D-U-N-S Number, payments profile, organizational information, contact information, identity verification, and merchant/bank verification when monetizing through Google Play.

This should be handled early because the public developer identity becomes part of the trust users associate with Mannerly.

## Standardize the App Identity

Use one permanent naming convention across the entire platform.

A practical structure would be:

Mannerly — public brand name

`mannerly.com` — public website

`app.mannerly.com` — web application

`support.mannerly.com` — support/help center

`schools.mannerly.com` — optional school portal

`com.mannerly.app` — production mobile application identifier

Internally, maintain separate environments for development, staging, and production.

Development should contain test users and experimental content.

Staging should mirror the production architecture and be used for final QA.

Production should contain real users and purchases.

Never test major billing, parent/child permissions, classroom access, region entitlements, or account deletion for the first time against the live environment.

## Central Entitlement System

Mannerly should maintain one central entitlement layer that answers questions such as:

Does this person have Free access?

What is their Home Region?

Do they have Manners+?

Are they part of a Family plan?

Which Travel Packs do they own?

Are they covered by a school license?

Which classroom memberships are active?

The storefront processes the transaction, but the Mannerly backend determines what the authenticated user can access.

This becomes especially important because Apple, Google, Amazon, Samsung, web payments, school invoices, promo codes, complimentary memberships, and future partnerships may all create legitimate access to the same curriculum.

The entitlement layer should therefore translate different payment sources into common internal permissions such as `GLOBAL_CORE`, `HOME_REGION_US`, `MANNERLY_PLUS`, `FAMILY`, `JAPAN_TRAVEL_PACK`, or `SCHOOL_LICENSE`.

## Subscription Products

Keep the initial catalog simple.

The primary consumer products should remain Mannerly+ Monthly, Mannerly+ Annual, and Mannerly Family Annual.

Travel Packs should be one-time regional unlocks where the economics and store rules support them.

School and district licensing should primarily be administered through Mannerly's institutional web system rather than forcing schools to purchase dozens or hundreds of seats through consumer app-store subscriptions.

Apple supports auto-renewable subscriptions through subscription groups in App Store Connect, and the necessary agreements, banking information, and tax information must be configured before In-App Purchases can be properly offered and tested.

Google Play Billing similarly supports digital products and subscriptions and provides APIs for keeping purchase state synchronized with a backend.

Do not build subscription access as a simple Boolean such as `premium=true`. Build a real entitlement system from the beginning.

## Apple App Store — Behind the Scenes

Create the Apple Developer organization account and establish the Mannerly application in App Store Connect.

Configure the production bundle identifier, signing credentials, push notification capabilities, subscription products, in-app purchases, tax and banking information, privacy information, age rating, territories, pricing, and required legal URLs.

Because Mannerly uses accounts, account deletion must be designed into the product before submission. Apple requires apps that support account creation to allow users to initiate account deletion from inside the application.

App Store Connect also requires the developer to disclose the application's data practices, including relevant data practices of integrated third-party SDKs, for the App Privacy information shown on the product page.

This means every analytics SDK, crash-reporting SDK, authentication provider, notification provider, payment integration, and other third-party service should be documented internally before submission.

For testing, use TestFlight. Apple supports internal and external beta distribution through TestFlight before production submission.

A sensible Apple release flow is:

development build → internal QA → TestFlight → parent/teacher/student beta testing → final privacy review → subscription testing → App Store submission → production rollout.

App Store Connect handles the app record, TestFlight distribution, submissions, agreements, financial information, and reporting.

If using Expo, EAS Build can manage signed production builds and EAS Submit can upload an iOS build into Apple's distribution workflow.

## Apple App Store — What Customers See

The public App Store presentation should immediately explain that Mannerly is for more than small children.

The app icon should use the simplified Mannerly two-person/checkmark mark.

The title should remain simply:

**Mannerly**

The subtitle or short positioning should communicate something close to:

**Manners. Confidence. Culture.**

The screenshot sequence should visually tell the product story.

The first screenshot should show an interactive scenario.

The next should show Global Manners.

Another should show the world/region exploration system.

Another should show the Mannerly Passport.

Another should show Family profiles.

Another should show classroom functionality.

Another should show Travel Packs.

The final screenshot should show progress, mastery, or achievements.

All screenshots should use the established Deep Blue, Mint Teal, Golden Yellow, Charcoal Navy, white-space-heavy visual system.

Avoid generic screenshots covered in explanatory text. Show the product actually being used.

The product page should emphasize:

**Learn what to do. Understand why. Feel confident anywhere.**

Localize the listing as additional interface languages are released rather than translating marketing materials for languages the actual product does not yet support.

## Children's Positioning on Apple

The Apple child strategy requires deliberate planning.

If Mannerly is placed in Apple's Kids Category, Apple applies additional Kids Category requirements including age-band selection, privacy limitations, and parental gates around certain actions.

Because Mannerly also serves teens, adults, parents, travelers, professionals, and teachers, the team should determine whether the primary Mannerly application should be positioned as an all-ages educational platform rather than designing the entire public product exclusively around Apple's Kids Category.

Regardless of store category, children's data should remain heavily minimized and parent-controlled.

The store configuration and the application's internal age-based experience must agree with each other.

## Google Play — Behind the Scenes

Create and verify the Mannerly organization developer account in Google Play Console.

Register the Android application, establish the permanent package identifier, configure Play App Signing, set up the payments profile, create subscription products, configure testing tracks, complete App Content declarations, complete the Data Safety section, establish age and target-audience settings, add the privacy policy, and prepare the production listing.

Google's Play App Signing system securely manages the application's signing key once configured.

Use internal testing first, followed by controlled closed testing before production. Google provides internal, closed, and open testing workflows; internal testing supports rapid distribution to a limited testing group.

Certain new personal developer accounts also face a required closed-testing period before gaining production access, another reason I would establish Mannerly as the proper organization account from the beginning.

Google requires published Play applications to complete the Data Safety form, and the disclosures must match what the application and its SDKs actually collect or share.

Because Mannerly includes children in its intended audience, its Google Play target-audience configuration must reflect that accurately. Apps including children in their target audience are subject to Google's Families Policy requirements.

For child or unknown-age users, Google also imposes restrictions around transmission of certain device and advertising identifiers.

This reinforces the earlier recommendation: **do not make advertising the core Mannerly business model.**

## Google Account Deletion

Google Play has an additional account architecture requirement that should influence the web product.

If an app lets people create accounts, Google requires an in-app path for requesting account deletion and also requires a web resource through which users can request account and associated-data deletion.

Mannerly should therefore build something like:

`mannerly.com/account/delete`

The signed-in app should also provide:

Settings → Account → Delete Account

Parent-owned child profiles should have a separate parent-controlled deletion workflow so deleting one learner profile does not accidentally delete the entire household account.

Teacher, student, and school data should have similarly explicit ownership and deletion rules.

## Google Play — What Customers See

The Play Store listing should closely match the Apple presentation so the brand remains consistent.

Use the same app icon.

Use the same core screenshot story.

Use the same positioning.

Keep screenshots slightly adapted to Android device dimensions rather than blindly reusing iPhone frames.

The Play listing should communicate three things immediately:

Mannerly teaches everyday social skills.

Mannerly teaches cultural etiquette by region.

Mannerly works for different ages and situations.

Parents should immediately see family functionality.

Teachers should immediately see classroom functionality.

Adults should immediately see travel, work, culture, and dining so they do not assume the application is only a children's product.

## Amazon Appstore

Amazon Appstore should be the first alternative Android marketplace I would evaluate after Apple, Google, and web, particularly if Mannerly decides to support Fire Tablet as a significant learning device.

Amazon uses its own Developer Console and application-submission process. Its In-App Purchasing system supports digital content and subscriptions, which means Mannerly would need to connect Amazon purchase receipts and entitlement events into the central Mannerly entitlement service.

Do not simply assume Google Play Billing will operate unchanged in the Amazon distribution version.

Create an Amazon-specific build and test profile.

Test:

account creation

family profiles

video and Rive animation performance

audio narration

offline lessons

notifications where supported

subscription purchase

subscription restoration

Travel Pack purchase

account deletion

child restrictions

tablet layouts

The public Amazon listing should remain visually identical to the Mannerly brand rather than becoming a separate Fire-branded product.

## Samsung Galaxy Store

Samsung Galaxy Store should be treated as an additional Android acquisition channel, not as a launch requirement.

Publishing is managed through Samsung Seller Portal. Samsung's developer documentation describes Seller Portal as the system for registering, publishing, managing, and promoting Galaxy Store apps, and commercial distribution can also involve seller and payment setup.

Samsung also maintains its own In-App Purchase system for Galaxy Store applications.

Therefore, add Samsung only when its expected user acquisition justifies maintaining another billing integration, testing matrix, listing, and review process.

## Huawei AppGallery

Huawei AppGallery should be considered when Mannerly begins targeting markets where Huawei distribution is strategically meaningful.

Huawei's process uses a verified HUAWEI ID and AppGallery Connect to create the application record, provide application details, upload the application package, and manage releases.

AppGallery Connect also supports product and in-app-purchase configuration.

Again, the important architectural rule is that Huawei users should still authenticate into the same Mannerly backend and receive the same learner profiles and curriculum entitlements.

## Microsoft Store

Microsoft Store is particularly interesting later for Mannerly's teacher, student, school, and desktop audiences.

Rather than building an entirely separate Windows application immediately, the Mannerly web application can eventually be packaged as a Progressive Web App.

Microsoft currently supports packaging a PWA using PWABuilder and submitting it through Partner Center to Microsoft Store.

That allows a school or Windows user to install Mannerly more like a desktop application while Mannerly continues maintaining the same underlying web product.

This should be considered a distribution enhancement rather than a separate product.

## Mannerly Web Application

The web experience should be a first-class product, not a reduced companion to the mobile application.

Use:

**mannerly.com**

for discovery, SEO, pricing, regional etiquette guides, travel content, school information, parent information, and marketing.

Use:

**app.mannerly.com**

for the authenticated learning application.

The web application should contain the same major learning functions as mobile:

onboarding

individual profiles

family accounts

child profiles

teacher dashboards

student lessons

Mannerly Passport

region selection

interactive scenarios

progress

subscriptions

Travel Packs

account management

accessibility settings

language preferences.

Because Mannerly previously selected Next.js for the web stack, it can be deployed through several production approaches including a Node.js server, containerized deployment, or supported hosting platforms.

The web application should also be built with Progressive Web App capabilities where practical. Current Next.js documentation supports PWA patterns, and installable PWAs can provide more app-like access while still running from the web codebase.

This means someone could discover Mannerly through Google, complete a free etiquette lesson, create an account, and continue using Mannerly without installing anything.

That is an important advantage over relying exclusively on app-store discovery.

## Web Payments

Web should become Mannerly's primary account-management surface.

Adults should be able to view their plan, family members, Travel Packs, billing status, privacy settings, account deletion, school relationships, languages, and regions from the web.

Use a reputable web payment processor for web purchases and have successful transactions write into the same centralized entitlement system used by mobile purchases.

Native applications should continue to comply with the current payment and digital-content rules of each storefront where they are distributed. Those policies can vary by platform, country, storefront program, and product type, so purchase flows should be reviewed against current store rules before each major release rather than hard-coding one global assumption.

## Teacher and School Web Dashboard

The teacher experience should be web-first even though lesson consumption remains cross-platform.

A teacher works more efficiently on a laptop when creating classrooms, assigning 30 students, reviewing completion, selecting lessons, managing curriculum, printing class codes, and viewing reports.

The teacher web dashboard should therefore provide:

class creation

student rosters

join codes

assignments

curriculum selection

regional packs

lesson preview

completion reporting

mastery reporting

accessibility accommodations

classroom language

license management

parent-connection permissions.

Students can then consume the assigned experience wherever they are: Chromebook browser, Windows computer, iPad, iPhone, Android phone, Fire Tablet, or other supported device.

## Parent Web Dashboard

Parents should similarly have a full web dashboard.

The parent should be able to log in and see all household learner profiles, assigned challenges, progress summaries, languages, accessibility settings, subscription status, regional access, purchases, and privacy controls.

This becomes especially valuable when a child's primary learning device is a tablet where detailed account administration would be inconvenient.

## Public SEO Strategy

Every major Mannerly curriculum area should have a public web presence.

Examples include pages for Japanese etiquette, restaurant manners, manners for children, workplace etiquette, table manners, digital manners, classroom manners, travel etiquette, conversation etiquette, Korean etiquette, Indian etiquette, Mexican etiquette, and similar topics.

Each page should provide real educational value for free and then transition naturally into:

**Practice this situation in Mannerly.**

This gives Mannerly a customer-acquisition system that the app stores alone cannot provide.

The funnel becomes:

Google/search/social content → free Mannerly lesson → personalized onboarding → account creation → Global Core + Home Region → continued learning → optional paid upgrade.

## Store Listing Assets

Create one reusable master asset library rather than recreating graphics during every release.

The library should include the full horizontal Mannerly logo, stacked logo, icon-only version, monochrome logo, dark-mode logo, application icon, screenshots, tablet screenshots, teacher screenshots, family screenshots, Travel Pack screenshots, device mockups, app-preview video assets, promotional banners, and press assets.

The same Deep Blue, Mint Teal, Golden Yellow, Charcoal Navy, rounded typography, characters, illustrations, and animation language should appear everywhere.

Someone should be able to move from a Mannerly advertisement to the website to the App Store to onboarding and feel that they never changed products.

